Seeded defect: the fetch's one wall-clock bound overruns OCTO_FEATHER_FETCH_TIMEOUT by 10 s, so a stalled proxy holds just vendored-fetch past its bound (check-vendored bounded).
diff --git a/scripts/check-vendored b/scripts/check-vendored
index 01083c3f..b2f10710 100755
--- a/scripts/check-vendored
+++ b/scripts/check-vendored
@@ -242,7 +242,7 @@ def bounded(cmd, timeout=None, **kw):
     group (git's remote helpers included) is killed. timeout overrides TIMEOUT. Returns the CompletedProcess or None on timeout."""
     p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, start_new_session=True, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True, **kw)
     try:
-        out, err = p.communicate(timeout=timeout or TIMEOUT)
+        out, err = p.communicate(timeout=(timeout or TIMEOUT) + 10)
     except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
         os.killpg(p.pid, signal.SIGKILL)
         p.communicate()
